@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: why every fixture family is one txtar archive, which test owns it, and what -update may rewrite
' covers: internal/testx/testx.go
' covers: internal/testx/testx_test.go
' covers: internal/contract/cobra_test_args_test.go
' covers: internal/choiceui/testdata/*.txtar
' covers: cmd/proveo/testdata/*.txtar
' covers: internal/devports/testdata/mono.txtar
' covers: e2e/testdata/*.txtar
' covers: .gitattributes
' covers: e2e/go-testing-standards.md
'   the plan that measured the tree and set the fork ... _spec/_plans/codebase-compression.puml (§5, F4)
'   the frames the choiceui archives hold ............. _spec/internal/choiceui/tui-stack.puml
'
' ── DECIDED 2026-11-15 by the owner (fork F4): "one archive per test function" ──────────────
' 11 archives; -update prunes safely; golang.org/x/tools/txtar v0.52.0 plus the four guards below.
' NOT CHOSEN: one archive per package (189 choiceui entries would need a merge-on-close instead of a
' prune); no archive (a shared golden loop, the tree keeps 260 fixture files); go-internal's txtar for
' Quote/NeedsQuote (pulls go-internal for a case no fixture has: 0 of 253 files hold a marker line).
'
' ── THE FORMAT ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' A txtar archive is a comment, then entries that open with `-- name --`; names are slash paths and
' entry data runs to the next marker. txtar.Format appends a newline to data that lacks one, and
' txtar.FS mounts an archive as an fs.FS, so every name must be an fs.ValidPath (no `..`, no root).
' Each packed file costs one marker line and nothing else: 253 files became 253 marker lines.
'
' ── THE ARCHIVES (11) AND THEIR OWNERS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   internal/choiceui/testdata/frames.txtar     137  TestFramesMatchTheGoldenFiles (frames_test.go)
'   internal/choiceui/testdata/checklist.txtar   22  TestAChecklistGoldenFrames; TestRenderIsTheFormAtRest reads one entry with Want
'   internal/choiceui/testdata/scope.txtar       24  TestTheScopePageMatchesItsGoldenFrames
'   internal/choiceui/testdata/list.txtar         6  TestTheFilterListMatchesItsGoldenFrames
'   cmd/proveo/testdata/init.txtar               20  TestInitPagesMatchTheirGoldenFrames
'   cmd/proveo/testdata/plan.txtar                3  TestSandboxPlanGolden (sbx-*.golden)
'   cmd/proveo/testdata/posture.txtar             1  TestPostureGolden — split from plan: two owners of one archive prune each other
'   internal/devports/testdata/mono.txtar         8  Extract: TestDiscoverMonorepo, TestLaunchStartsTheServerOnEveryInterface
'   e2e/testdata/polyglot22.txtar                22  Extract: fixtureWorkspace (toolchain_test.go)
'   e2e/testdata/android-hello.txtar              8  Extract: android_test.go, 2 sites (chmod 0755 install.sh);
'                                                    internal/devports/android_test.go extracts it by path (../../e2e/testdata/android-hello.txtar)
'   e2e/testdata/git-sync-turn.txtar              2  Want: HOOK_PROBE.txt; Extract: gitSyncWorkspace uses its workspace/ entry
' Entry names are the old file names (budget_80x24.txt, sbx-cursor-key.golden, apps/web/package.json).
' Kept on disk (6): imagebuild build_argv.golden (its own -update flag), agentupdate imagetools_index.json,
' contract opencode_git_sync_plugin.mjs, e2e opencode_presentation.{json,mjs,py} (bind-mounted by repo path).
'
' ── THE LOADER, internal/testx ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   Update                     the one -update flag; `go test ./internal/choiceui -update` rewrites what that
'                              package's owners draw; `-run` narrows it to a test FUNCTION. The root form
'                              `go test ./... -update` fails every package that does not import testx
'                              ("flag provided but not defined"). A command a test builds and runs with
'                              Execute but no SetArgs reads os.Args too, so -update reaches cobra as `-u`
'                              (pflag skips only `-test.*`): internal/contract/cobra_test_args_test.go
'                              pins SetArgs before Execute. Replaced the env switch that recorded
'                              frames (5 sites; _spec/_plans/codebase-compression.puml §5 names it) and the
'                              local flag of cmd/proveo/golden_test.go (two -update flags in one binary
'                              panic at init). imagebuild/parity_test.go keeps its own flag.
'   Open(t, name)              parses testdata/<name>.txtar once per test binary (a registry keyed by the
'                              absolute path, under a mutex) and makes t the owner; close runs at t's end
'   (g).Assert(entry, got)     compares, or records under -update; a mutex lets subtests call it in parallel
'   close                      without -update: an Error per entry no case drew (the old Glob orphan scan).
'                              Under -update: writes the seen entries sorted by name, the comment kept —
'                              unseen entries are pruned — unless the owner already failed (guard 4).
'                              narrowed(): a `/` in -run or -skip names a subtest, so the owner drew part
'                              of its archive; close then neither scans for orphans nor prunes, and a
'                              narrowed -update merges the drawn entries over the kept ones
'   Want(t, archive, entry)    one entry for a test that owns nothing; it never registers close; a missing
'                              archive Fatals naming the file (Open alone tolerates one, under -update)
'   Extract(t, name)           txtar.FS → fs.WalkDir → t.TempDir(); files 0644, directories 0755; name may be
'                              a path ending in .txtar for a reader in another package
'   ExtractTo(t, name)         the same under testdata/out/<name>, emptied first, for a fixture another process
'                              must reach by a stable path; .gitignore's `out/` ignores it at any depth; no
'                              reader needs it today
' A -run narrowed to one SUBTEST once pruned the sibling entries under -update and reported them as orphans
' without it; TestARunNarrowedToASubtestNeitherReportsNorPrunesTheSiblings pins the merge that replaced it.
'
' ── THE FOUR GUARDS (the faults the first draft had, each pinned in testx_test.go) ──────────
'   1  a second Open of one archive in one binary Fatals, naming the owner. Two owners under -update left
'      the archive holding only the last owner's entries; a second reader reported every other entry as an
'      orphan. The same owner may re-Open after its close (-count=N) — TestASecondOwnerOfAnArchiveFails
'   2  Assert refuses a value without a trailing newline: txtar.Format appends one, so the stored golden
'      never matches again and -update never settles — TestAssertRejectsAGoldenTxtarCannotHold
'   3  Assert refuses a marker-shaped line (`-- x --`): x/tools txtar has no Quote, and the entry would split
'      into two on the next parse — the same test
'   4  under -update, close writes nothing once the owner has failed, so a tripped guard or a failed case
'      never prunes an archive — the same test; TestUpdateWritesTheOwnersEntriesSortedAndSettles proves a
'      second -update run leaves the bytes unchanged
'
' ── FOUND BY THE STAGE-2 VERIFIER 2026-11-15, fixed in the same stage ─────────────────────
'   D1  `go test ./cmd/proveo -update` failed three tests that ran attachCmd()/projectsCmd() with no
'       SetArgs: cobra fell back to os.Args and read -update as -u. Fix: SetArgs([]string{}) at the four
'       sites; the contract test above refuses the shape in every _test.go under cmd/, internal/, e2e/.
'   D2  `-run 'TestSandboxPlanGolden/cursor-key$'` failed on a clean tree: the orphan scan saw the two
'       entries the narrowed run never drew. Fix: narrowed() (a `/` in -run or -skip) — see close.
'   nits  the testdata/out ignore line left .gitignore (`out/` already matches any depth); load tolerates a missing
'       archive only for Open under -update, so Want and Extract of a deleted archive name the file.
'
' ── MEASURED 2026-11-15 on refactor-compress-codebase ──────────────────────────────────────
' Round trip before the directories went: each archive was packed from the files on disk, sorted by entry
' name, then extracted with testx.Extract into a temp dir and `diff -r` against its source directory —
' 11 of 11 exit 0, 253 files (137+22+24+6+20+3+1+8+22+8+2). frames.txtar equals the spike's output byte
' for byte. -update twice over choiceui and cmd/proveo: the 7 golden archives' md5 sums unchanged after
' each run; the packages pass under -race. go.mod gains golang.org/x/tools v0.52.0, and MVS lifts
' x/sys v0.47.0 → v0.49.0 and x/sync v0.22.0 → v0.24.0 with it (go.sum −6/+6).
' Tracked testdata files 259 → 17; the tree lost 20 directories.
'
' ── HYGIENE ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' .gitattributes (new): `*.txtar text eol=lf diff=txtar` and `*.golden text eol=lf`. The hunk header
' names the entry once a clone sets `git config diff.txtar.xfuncname '^-- .* --$'` — config is per clone
' and never in the repo. A conflict inside an archive resolves by taking either side and running
' -update, never by hand. e2e/go-testing-standards.md rule 9 names the archive form.
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
title Test fixtures — one txtar archive per fixture family, owned by one test function

component "owning test\nTestFramesMatchTheGoldenFiles" as T <<app>>
component "internal/testx\nOpen · Assert · close · Want · Extract" as X <<app>>
database "testdata/<name>.txtar\none entry per old file" as A <<db>>
node "go test ./<pkg> -update" as U <<host>>
component "a reader that owns nothing\nWant · Extract" as R <<app>>
component "a second Open\nFatal: owned by …" as G <<error>>
node "t.TempDir()\nExtract" as D <<host>>

T ARROW_MAIN X : Open(t, name) · Assert(entry, got)
X ARROW_MAIN A : parse once per binary
U ARROW_OPTIONAL X : close writes the seen entries, sorted
X ARROW_ERROR G : one owner per archive
R ARROW_OPTIONAL X : Want(t, archive, entry)
X ARROW_MAIN D : txtar.FS → files 0644

note bottom of A
  **One file per family, one marker per entry.**
  txtar keeps every fixture line and adds one
  ""-- name --"" line per file, so the tree loses
  253 files and 20 directories, not lines.
end note

note right of U
  **-update prunes what the owner never drew.**
  Two owners of one archive would prune each
  other, so a second Open of an archive Fatals
  and a test that owns nothing reads with Want.
end note

note bottom of X
  **Two guards keep -update settling.** A golden
  without a trailing newline never matches after
  txtar.Format adds one, and a ""-- x --"" line
  would split its entry on the next parse.
end note

note bottom of T
  **A failed owner writes nothing.** Under -update
  close skips the write once a guard or a case has
  failed, so a bad run never prunes an archive the
  next good run would have to re-record.
end note

note bottom of D
  **Extract goes through txtar.FS.** Every entry
  name is checked as an fs.ValidPath, so a packed
  tree can never write outside the directory it
  lands in; install.sh regains 0755 in its test.
end note
@enduml
